    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of what was completed:\n\n## Implementation Complete \u2705\n\n### Core Functionality Added:\n\n**frai-core/src/eval/index.js**\n- `validateThreshold()`: Parses and validates `metric=number` format thresholds\n- `evaluateThresholds()`: Evaluates metrics against thresholds, returns pass/fail results\n- Modified `generateReport()` to accept optional thresholds and include results in reports\n\n**frai-cli/src/index.ts**\n- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option (can be used multiple times)\n- Implemented threshold validation with proper error handling\n- Exit codes: 0 (pass), 1 (fail), 2 (usage error)\n\n**Report Enhancements**\n- JSON reports: New top-level `passed` field and `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries\n- Markdown reports: New \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status\n\n**Documentation**\n- Updated `frai eval` documentation with threshold option details\n\n### Tested Scenarios:\n- \u2705 Single and multiple thresholds\n- \u2705 Passing thresholds \u2192 exit 0, report shows `passed: true`\n- \u2705 Failing thresholds \u2192 exit 1, report shows `passed: false`\n- \u2705 Metrics with no score \u2192 threshold fails automatically\n- \u2705 Invalid format \u2192 exit 2, shows usage error\n- \u2705 Unknown metric \u2192 exit 2, lists valid metrics\n- \u2705 Backward compatible (no thresholds = unchanged behavior)\n- \u2705 Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`\n\nThe implementation is complete with all specified requirements met. The two test failures in the suite are pre-existing issues unrelated to this feature.",
